```java
String user = request.getParameter("user");  // attacker types: ' OR '1'='1
String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '" + user + "'";
// becomes: SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '' OR '1'='1'  <- always true!
Statement st = con.createStatement();
ResultSet rs = st.executeQuery(sql);   // returns ALL users -> auth bypass
```

```java
String user = request.getParameter("user");
String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = ?";
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql)) {
    ps.setString(1, user);   // ' OR '1'='1 is treated as a literal string
    ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery();  // matches a user literally named that
}
```

*The driver sends SQL and data separately, so input can never become executable SQL.*
